+# SOCC recording and document-save entries: precise preservation leads
+
+October30,2026. TEL02/TEL04, AUD016-A1 and TEL-NI-TIME. Further selected reading of the [public AA SOC/SOCC log reader](https://www.scribd.com/document/16762194/T7-B20-Timelines-911-2-of-2-Fdr-AA-SOCC-Log-Redacted-Version) supplies a recording-retrieval entry and a separate native-document label. These are source-reported activities in a mirror, not authenticated native files or independently established preservation outcomes.
+
+## Two different save-related records
+
+**1343, viewer p6 / AA KEAN COMM002535:** the entry describes staff accessing recorded calls into SOC, with files to be saved once found. This identifies a concrete retrieval and preservation trail: the work request/log, recording system and call identifiers, search outcome, copied-media/file manifest and retention/delivery records. It does not establish that calls were found or saved, identify which conversation, prove continued existence or join any court audio derivative. The [November interview's p4 tape-counter/second-recording account](https://catalog.archives.gov/medialive/0/6096/2609600/content/arcmedia/9-11/MFR/t-0148-911MFR-00014.pdf#page=4) remains a separate source claim with its own untested continuity.
+
+**1739, p6 / the same Bates page:** a later entry reports saving the file up to that point under the visible label reading **`Accident_1738/11sep.doc`**. Preserve that reading, including the apparent separator; native spelling, filesystem/path structure and actual format are independently unverified. A label ending.doc is not proof the recording files were saved. The underlying document, revisions and Commission attachment/delivery mapping are specific new targets. No native DOC was acquired or hashed. One exact-component indexed query returned no locator; that is not proof of absence, withholding or destruction.
+
+The p6 footer actually observed reads **6of32**, **AA KEAN COMM002535**, **1/15/02 7:21**. The last is a visible print/export label, not authenticated native creation time, a source clock or complete version history. We do not infer that the1739save denotes the final32-page version or the exact chronology used at the2003interview.
+
+## Qualifications supplied by the surrounding source
+
+- **0930, p5 / AA KEAN COMM002534:** an entry explicitly calls the codeshare-notification time an estimate. It appears below0955 and an un-timed entry. Preserve the order and qualifier; this does not measure a clock error, actual dispatch or recipient receipt. It also does not make every table time an estimate.
+- **0015 /12Sep, p7:** the source reports a security directive communicated by conference and a written directive still pending. Verbal notification, written issue and field implementation need different records. This next-day entry cannot establish9/11cockpit-warning delivery or the later May2003QFR/2006disposition outcomes.
+- **1743 across pp6-7:** the sentence about eliminating Flight11and77 continues with **schedule** at the top of p7. Keep that object with its sentence. The earlier [p3 row0748 ASD-removal request](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/b4c559927c95180b96870112374910a0af15d65e/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-socc-log-reader-2026-10-30/README.md), the1343recording entry and the1739document-save label remain separate. No common deletion operation or actual disposal follows.
+
+The strongest limitation is the missing source/version/call join: a later exported log can report a plan or action without proving native bytes, success or delivery. Conversely, those limits do not justify discarding its exact retrieval targets. Source-specific originals, negative results and contrary records could strengthen or weaken the interpretation.
+
+## Actual scope and preservation
+
+Inspected selected upper/lower regions of p5, p6 upper and lower/footer, p7 upper/middle and dated continuation, and p8 upper/middle. **No complete four-page or32-page reading is claimed**; intervening/later regions remain uninspected. No finding of absence is based on those unread portions. No audio was played or decoded, no clock fitted, no carrier/caller join tested and no physical experiment performed.
+
+The source remains a public third-party reader, not an authenticated native log or official release counterpart. Native PDF bytes/hash remain unknown; download/login gates were not bypassed. Only two code-free browser JPEG derivatives were saved separately locally, with role-qualified hash pins. Raw images, full text/OCR, signatures, personal/contact/account and access-code fields are excluded from publication. Other tool-view frames were not copied into new raw-image files because they contain excluded fields. Selected manual time/filename observations are independently qualified; no hidden text or redacted identity was reconstructed.
+
+[SOURCE-PINS.json](SOURCE-PINS.json) records source URL, exact row/page/Bates and actual reading/hash limits. [OBSERVATIONS-AND-TODOS.json](OBSERVATIONS-AND-TODOS.json), RF01-RF05, preserves observations, different event/object roles, falsifiers and missing originals. [CHECKLIST.json](CHECKLIST.json) accounts for this unit; [PROVENANCE-CHECKS.json](PROVENANCE-CHECKS.json) records the actual narrow checks without calling them historical validation. [TEXT-CHANGES.diff](TEXT-CHANGES.diff) is the actual addition diff at a new path. [MANIFEST.json](MANIFEST.json) pins the other six files. Previous sources and conflicting records were not changed.
+
+A parallel local readiness audit retains all18 original acceptance criteria. This source check advances precise original-record targets; it closes none of those criteria. Publication, file counts and hashes are separate from substantive completion. The FAA correction/receipt/signed-disposition, telephone native joins, technical-owner recorder/materials inputs and steel native custody/attribution/review records remain open/partial. No outreach, fees, new request/filing, mailbox/private-case use, raw publication, private push, deletion or history rewrite occurred.
